==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Bun Bun Monger Iron''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Bun Bun Monger Devil''' at level 20 after clearing the final stage of [[Empire of Cats]] Chapter 3.

==Strategy/Usage==
This cat is supposed to be a tank, with its movement speed, as it can rush in and deliver its damage while tanking some hits before dying. Unfortunately, as with many [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]], this unit has low overall stats, and is only useful if maxed out using [[Catseye]]s.

Considering its low overall range and health, it is safe to say in all mid-game scenarios, Bun Bun Monger will not last long enough in battle to contribute anything of worthwhile note. It would just be better to use another cat if you want a [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rusher]]; [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] being the most ideal. Even [[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Lion Cat]] would be better, since it can be spammed, and doesn't cost as much.

In the best of all cases, Bun Bun Monger is passable at rushing in and beating '''very''' early Four Star [[Legend Stages|Stories of Legend]] subchapters, or at least being a source of DPS. However, this assumes you do not have any better sources of DPS to work with, and you most certainly will, as the spammability of cats like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] and [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] outclass him.

==='''True Form'''===
Bun Bun Monger Devil gains the ability to survive lethal strikes at a 100% chance, along with a slight improvement of his base stats. Similarly to its [[Mecha-Bun (Special Cat)|mobile counterpart]], it has low base stats and only a slight improvement in [[True Form]]. The difference between the two is, this one has half the health of its mobile form, and because of its short range, the [[Survive]] ability improves nothing.

{{Job|Classification = User Rank Dump & Rusher}}

